{
 "source": {
  "commit": "28eaf9455bad6ff52dcbdbc29ecc07d7dde83e2a",
  "how": "dataclasses.asdict(devloop.config.load_config()) and review_policy.version(), computed by the code and the devloop/config.toml of that commit (origin/main before ADR 0006, R3), without overlay nor project file; tuples written as lists",
  "updated": "later changes of the installation, not R3's, added to config.toml and here with only the values they add (the policy version does not change): [apps.implementer], implementers and agents.*.app (issue #407, PR #442); delegations.capacity and capacity_max_* (issue #412, PR #450); [tests], the selection of the test modules and the format of the CI logs that the code of that commit had built in (devloop/localtests.py), declared since ADR 0006, R5 (issue #424); agents.*.provider, provider of the fallbacks and review_policy.provider_quorum (issue #409); review_policy.fallback_provider_ban (issue #410); delegations.budget (issue #411, PR #449); review_policy.findings_reviewer (issue #416); delegations.merge, max_merges_per_day and merge_trust_paths (issue #486); review_policy.second_reviewer, parallel by default (issue #521); agent_user.cli_denied, the entries of the CLIs of the agent user that the configuration takes away from the list of the code, none by default (issue #517); roles.coordinator, the coordinator actor, off (null) by default (issue #528); repo_aliases, the former names of the repository, none by default (issue #540); max_requested_fix_rounds, the rounds after a /devloop fix of a trusted user on an approved head that do not count, 2 by default, the cap of the code (issue #536); conclave_substitute_timeout_seconds, how long a conclave waits for the coordinator's substitute vote, 7200 by default (issue #605); state_dir, .devloop instead of .ssdlc/devloop, out of the state directory of the old SSDLC engine (issue #563), the value of the installation replaced, not added; direction.issue, the issue of the operator's direction, none (0) by default (issue #604); notify, the channel of the notices to the operator, none by default, and operator_mentions, the logins mentioned in the requests for a decision, none by default (issue #593), keys of the overlay only; labels.needs_coordinator, the label of the issues waiting for the coordinator's /devloop authorize, agent:needs-coordinator by default, a default of the code with the other labels, which have no table in config.toml (issue #607); run.rest_dir and run.rest_wake_timeout, the directory of the roles' rest, none (empty) by default, and the seconds devloop run waits for a role at rest to wake up before telling the operator, 300 by default (issue #684), keys of the overlay only; prepare, the step that prepares a worktree, none (an empty command) by default (issue #696);the keys by role of the agents, claude-implementer, codex-reviewer and agy-reviewer with their app and provider, and claude-reviewer, the third reviewer, last in the pool (issue #499): unlike the others, these change the policy version, which is updated with them; and a change of ssdlc's values, not of the installation: the SSDLC engine left main (ADR 0007, R1, issue #538), and with it its sensitive paths, the list of the replay gate's baseline (sensitive_path_lists, so sensitive_files and the list among pin.paths), the prefix ssdlc_ of tests.source_prefixes and the entries of the engine in docs.map, removed from config.toml and here; these change the policy version too, which is updated with them; and another change of ssdlc's values: the entries \"ops/\" and \"docs/devloop/roles/\" of tests.dir_modules, which select tests/test_ops.py (issue #615), added to config.toml and here"
 },
